INTAFACED — THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTION AND LICENCE RECORD
======================================================

This file records every third-party component this repository redistributes,
builds against, or loads at runtime, together with the licence each component
actually declares and the evidence that declaration was read from.

Compiled: 2026-07-29, against commit 4311cff.

WHAT THIS FILE IS
-----------------

An engineering record. It is not legal advice, it is not a legal opinion, and
it does not clear anything for launch. It states what is in the tree and what
each artefact says about itself. Decisions and the work required before launch
are in `docs/LICENCE-POSITION.md`.

Two rules were applied without exception while compiling it:

  1. A licence is recorded only where it was read from the artefact itself, or
     from the published POM of the exact version the build resolves. Nothing
     was inferred from a project's reputation, popularity or usual terms.

  2. Where provenance could not be established, the entry says UNDETERMINED and
     states exactly what was checked. An invented attribution is a false legal
     statement and is worse than an admission of ignorance.

`vendor/upstream-exchange/NOTICE` and `vendor/upstream-exchange/LICENSE` are the upstream
provenance record and are unmodified. This file adds to them; it does not
replace or correct them.

SCOPE OF "REDISTRIBUTE"
-----------------------

Three different things are called "a dependency" below, and they carry
different obligations:

  REDISTRIBUTED IN THIS REPOSITORY — the bytes are committed here. Anyone who
  receives a clone receives them. §1 to §5.

  LOADED AT RUNTIME FROM A THIRD PARTY — the bytes are fetched from someone
  else's server when a page runs. Not redistributed, but executed in our users'
  browsers under our domain. §6.

  RESOLVED AT BUILD TIME — the bytes are pulled from a package registry during
  a build and end up inside a built image or bundle. Not committed here, but
  redistributed by any image we ship. §7 and §8.


